# GitHub PR Target

This checkout has exactly one git remote:

- `origin` = `unfoldingWord-box3/BPtranslate`

(The repo moved there from `deferredreward/bible-editor-multilingual` on 2026-09-16. Old URLs redirect, but don't write new ones.)

It is still a GitHub **fork** of `unfoldingWord/bible-editor`, deliberately — detaching the fork network would drop every issue and PR. Upstream is a **read-only source we cherry-pick from; it must never receive a PR from this repo.** There is no `upstream` git remote; upstream syncs fetch the URL directly (`git fetch https://github.com/unfoldingWord/bible-editor main`) and are recorded in `docs/upstream-sync-*.md`.

Because the fork relationship still exists, the GitHub CLI may resolve a bare `gh pr create` / `gh pr view` / `gh issue ...` to the parent repo. Always pass the repository explicitly:

```powershell
gh pr create --repo unfoldingWord-box3/BPtranslate --base main
gh pr view --repo unfoldingWord-box3/BPtranslate
gh issue list --repo unfoldingWord-box3/BPtranslate
```

Never accept a PR URL under `github.com/unfoldingWord/bible-editor` for this workspace unless the user explicitly asks to target upstream.
